{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512974-do-you-think-that-a-vampire-can-create-a-mortal-clone-of-themselves","id":1512974,"title":"Do you think that a vampire can create a mortal clone of themselves?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-27T10:05:40-07:00","id":1512974,"title":"Do you think that a vampire can create a mortal clone of themselves?","content":"It's just a curious notion in that in many instances that some of these elders and ancients are the only branch of there mortal families that are still around and that may weigh heavily on some of them as they know that final death could come for them and that's it the family line is gone and they may want something to carry on .<br /> <br /> It's just something that came to me when Shovelhead3 post on Kindred nature got me thinking. Do you think anyone of them might discretely try and attempt it and the masqerade be damned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-03-2023, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T10:50:36-07:00","id":1512983,"title":"","content":"In Gehenna Saulot was cloned<br /> the Child of Gaia geneticist Cernonous, has sought ways to restore the Bunyip. As the kin of the Bunyip is extinct, Cernonous begun to clone thylacines from stolen genetic material from exhibitions, and discovering a piece of Bunyip DNA in 2000. Using spirit magics of the Weaver, he managed to make these thylacines mate, and they produced a set of cubs that smelled like Garou, although a bit different. These cubs under went the First Change after merely two years and formed a provisional pack on their own. In one scenario of the Apocalypse, Cernonous's &quot;Bunyip&quot; reveal that they do not possess a spiritual half like other Garou, Cernonous was only able to recreate the animal and the human nature of the Bunyip, and the lacking spiritual bits were filled by Wyrm-spirits that noticed his experiment. These Bunyip, calling themselves the Hollow Walkers, forced their father to walk the Black Spiral and join them\u200b<br /> So... yeah<br /> The technology exist in WoD (well not just in wod, In 2018, the first successful cloning of primates using SCNT was reported with the birth of two live female clones, crab-eating macaques named Zhong Zhong and Hua Hua) the rest is just the question of money and ethical dilemmas - one the Vampires have plenty and one they usually lacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T10:55:02-07:00","id":1512984,"title":"","content":"Mabye with very high ( 6+ ) levels of Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> There are some optional rules about preserving vampire body parts in Winter's Teeth - issue 3 ( the chapter about those renegade ghouls who steal vampire body parts and graft them on themselves ) but it's V5 rules.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, a ghoul with advanced medical equipement and very high Willpower, not to mention a limitless supply of Vitae, mabye could do that in a rather grisly way.<br /> A ghoul can regenerate limbs and even organs as if they were aggravated damage.<br /> Assuming he has a lab, medical equipement and retainers with specialized skills, he could slowly assemble a cloned body by having parts of himself removed and kept alive in vats, while he should be kept alive by machines untill he regenerated the vital parts harvested. Even the brain, one piece at time.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> By the way, talking about clones, what happened to the Samuel Haight's clone made by the technocracy in the end?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-27-2023, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T12:02:22-07:00","id":1512991,"title":"","content":"This would be a interesting ethical problem as would said kindred try to be a presence in his or her clone's life and try to make things easier or if it was me. I would keep a discrete distance not to bring my baggage into the mix and put my clone's life in danger from rivals who would love to stick it to me. I would try to make sure he would be placed in a good home and watch from a distance for sometime. No such thing as an easy answer to this notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:35:07-07:00","id":1513582,"title":"","content":"In theory it is not only possible but relatively easy. Without considering any supernatural abilities or blood sorceries, a vampire is technically a being trapped in a state between being a living organism and being a corpse. And preserved corpses still have dna, as some can found in bones and mummies. So finding dna from vampires would only requires the same techniques as those used by police and archeologists to extract dna from dead people.<br /> <br /> Now that you got your dna, you can use it to create a clone, either through a surrogate mother, or, if you're rich/connected enough, you can try for a prototype of artificial uterus.<br /> <br /> <br /> The preferred method would then depend on the goals of the vampire. Someone wanting an ongoing family would favorise having clones born from surrogates, another merely wanting living people to impersonate in the daylight society might favorise more high tech ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T17:11:02-07:00","id":1513585,"title":"","content":"Not Cloning per se, but it would be a potential way to produce a mortal lineage post embrace.<br /> <br /> Use Path of Conjuring to produce a living mortal clone, use Dominate to possess the clone. Collect reproductive material from the clone and use IVF techniques to fertilize some eggs. The clone itself only lasts about a week and then fades away. If we extrapolate this mechanic to relate to the genetic material, that would mean only the initial DNA strands would fade since all the follow up cells would be constructed from non-magical materials. Then you just put the fertilized eggs into surrogate women and see how things turn out, with some luck they carry to term and produce healthy mortal offspring. Theoretically once implantation is successful the pregnancy would proceed normally. But if there are complications, I assume that ghouling the mother would override most medical issues. Admittedly, this could mean the production of a Revenant bloodline rather than an exclusively mortal one, if carried on as a very long experiment.<br /> <br /> The fact that Path of Conjuration creates what you desire means that technically a female Thaumaturge could produce a gender swapped or hermaphroditic clone to produce the required sperm. You could skip the Dominate requirement and just farm the clone body manually, but I figure most vampires who are fixated enough to try to create a mortal lineage would want a more active role in all this and enjoy it. Furthermore, having high level Dominate means you more or less have your pick of potential breeding partners for your experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:10:51-07:00","id":1513595,"title":"","content":"At my table, I would say that purely via science, no. A vampire is an unnatural, cursed mostly dead being animated by magic. I'd say attempts to use the vampire's DNA would to create a clone would fail. It wouldn't take or begin replication. If the vampire had any DNA left from their mortal pre-embrace, that could be used and it would be no different than say, having someone who donated sperm before becoming a vampire end up having that sperm used. If a vampire wanted to use their own vampiric DNA to create a clone, they'd need to use thaumaturgy or some sort of supernatural magic to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:28:09-07:00","id":1513680,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if a vampire's supernatural state would prevent it from being done, but I would like to think of it being possible in my head cannon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:19:17-07:00","id":1513709,"title":"","content":"I suppose with a genetic material it would be possible, but I imagine there would be complications and the big question is, why would they do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:54:05-07:00","id":1513713,"title":"","content":"Didn't Beckett's Jyhad Diary mention that kindred have no DNA? Like the embrace erases it or something...<br /> <br /> The only things that come to mind are that you can use vicissitude to make a mortal look like you. Path of conjuring has been mentioned. Biothaumaturgy? Changelings can probably get you a chimerical clone, but that will be useless outside of the Dreaming... unless a Ravnos elder makes it? If your concern is the family lineage, not just having a clone, then perhaps you can use blood magic to sire a dhampir baby... You could try and get the aid of awakened magic? Or selling your soul off in an infernal pact in exchange for a baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T10:36:13-07:00","id":1513791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512974-do-you-think-that-a-vampire-can-create-a-mortal-clone-of-themselves?p=1513709#post1513709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose with a genetic material it would be possible, but I imagine there would be complications and the big question is, why would they do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion came to me when ShovelHead3 post about Schdanfraude got me thinking and the clan Lasombra trilogy where Montano went back to his homeland and found to his shock that his tribe no longer existed and then what if your an ancient kindred that has seen his or her family line die out and they are the only thing left and final death can come and that's it.<br /> <br /> Even monsters might still feel a connection to there mortal roots and want to see it continue in some form and thus this topic if they would try to create a clone of themselves and ensure there line would continue even if they suffer final death. It's an ethical deliemma for sure and Kindred can be very ruthless and foolish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-03-2023, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T13:44:35-07:00","id":1513808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512974-do-you-think-that-a-vampire-can-create-a-mortal-clone-of-themselves?p=1513791#post1513791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The notion came to me when ShovelHead3 post about Schdanfraude got me thinking and the clan Lasombra trilogy where Montano went back to his homeland and found to his shock that his tribe no longer existed and then what if your an ancient kindred that has seen his or her family line die out and they are the only thing left and final death can come and that's it.<br /> <br /> Even monsters might still feel a connection to there mortal roots and want to see it continue in some form and thus this topic if they would try to create a clone of themselves and ensure there line would continue even if they suffer final death. It's an ethical deliemma for sure and Kindred can be very ruthless and foolish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I understand partially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T12:40:16-07:00","id":1513888,"title":"","content":"Like I said. It\u2019s an interesting notion to consider for a game and possible storyline to use in a possible game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T14:44:23-07:00","id":1513894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512974-do-you-think-that-a-vampire-can-create-a-mortal-clone-of-themselves?p=1513713#post1513713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Beckett's Jyhad Diary mention that kindred have no DNA? Like the embrace erases it or something...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Been a while since I've read it, do you remember where in the book that detail might be?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:34:13-07:00","id":1513963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512974-do-you-think-that-a-vampire-can-create-a-mortal-clone-of-themselves?p=1513894#post1513894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Been a while since I've read it, do you remember where in the book that detail might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I might've been wrong. I remembered something from Netchurch's research of thinbloods and dhampirs, but what it specifically says is that he found traces of DNA in one thinblood's vitae rather than the usual amount of none at all.<br /> <br /> I think that got crossed with recollections of an older book I remember, which said that vampires have no fingerprints and, I think I remember it saying, leave no traceable forensic evidence at all (so no DNA). Assuming I didn't dream it, I <i>think</i> that was one of the older storyteller's guides, but I don't have that book anymore, so unless someone can confirm I'm not imagining things, my information's not trustworthy unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}